.TH MKTEMP 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
mktemp \- make a file or directory with a unique name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mktemp
.RB [ \-d ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.RI [ template ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mktemp
makes a new, empty file (or, with
.BR \-d ,
a directory) with a name nothing else has, and prints its name.
.PP
The trailing
.BR X s
of
.I template
(there must be at least 3) are replaced by random letters and digits;
names are tried until one is free (up to 100 tries). With no
.IR template ,
.B tmp.XXXXXXXXXX
is used, in the directory given by
.BR \-p ,
else in
.B $TMPDIR
or, if that is not set,
.IR /tmp .
A
.I template
that is given is taken as a path from the current directory, unless
.B \-p
or
.B \-t
names a directory for it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Make a directory, not a file.
.TP
.BI \-p " dir"
Put a
.I template
that has no
.B /
in
.IR dir .
.TP
.B \-t
Put a
.I template
that has no
.B /
in
.B $TMPDIR
or
.IR /tmp .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a bad option, too few
.BR X s,
or if nothing could be made.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
f=$(mktemp)
dir=$(mktemp \-d)
mktemp \-t build.XXXXXX
.fi
.SH NOTES
There is no
.B \-u
or
.BR \-q .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkdir (1),
.BR touch (1),
.BR rm (1)
